{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193105-vampires-blood-and-jewish-law","id":1193105,"title":"Vampires, Blood, and Jewish Law","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T07:28:39-08:00","id":1193105,"title":"Vampires, Blood, and Jewish Law","content":"I found an interesting thead linked to from RPGNet about how Jewish religious law would apply to vampires drinking blood:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/avatar_eef2a564fa30_128.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144\" target=\"_blank\"> Reblog by @alternativetodiscourse </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144\" target=\"_blank\"> https://alternativetodiscourse.tumblr.com/post/153238039722/animatedamerican-bigsis144 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 58&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 20202&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 25660&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Okay, so I asked my rabbi about this (... yes, my actual rabbi). Short answer, @fenrisesque\u200b, is that the ideal situation is for the vampire to intravenously ingest blood&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some of the conclusions might be surprising (such as human blood being more lawful than animal blood in all circumstances).<br /> <br /> <br /> Further down, when the vampire topic is done, it gets into how the law might apply in space, which could inspire how characters might view some of the otherworlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:43:29-08:00","id":1193295,"title":"","content":"That was one of the best trends I've ever read. Unexpected, academic, and playful in the purest sense (total engagement with the trivial.)<br /> <br /> I am jelly of the Jews now (for their cool rabbi support. I need to test a Catholic priest with a similar question and compare coolness ratings), and want to make a Vampire character that is Jewish, who regularly laments how his existence vindicates horrible anti-Jewish propaganda (blood-libel) even though his studies show it really is coincidental and that the propaganda really is just horrible antisemitism. The profound irritation would likely be a very memorable character quirk. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:50:06-08:00","id":1193296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cI don\u2019t know enough about vampire biology to tell you whether this is a viable solution\u201d - is something I did not expect to ever hear a rabbi say </div> </div> </div> Also not something I ever expected to read. To be fair, it would depend on the setting. Don't think it works with Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:31:22-08:00","id":1193308,"title":"","content":"That reminds me that I should write my version for a &quot;jewish derived&quot; covenant sometime :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:41:06-08:00","id":1193396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193105-vampires-blood-and-jewish-law?p=1193308#post1193308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me that I should write my version for a &quot;jewish derived&quot; covenant sometime :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been struggling with one too, wasn't really sure how to approach it - but link provides some nice hooks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:56:06-08:00","id":1193553,"title":"","content":"There was another post in there about using the Mourner's Prayer to counter a vampire instead of a cross or whatever. I like that, maybe a good bane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:38:38-08:00","id":1193879,"title":"","content":"If I'm reading that right then it doesn't apply to kindred because they don't breath and therefore are not alive however as fire does require oxygen it would count as alive? This gives that bane some interesting symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:04:16-08:00","id":1194172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193105-vampires-blood-and-jewish-law?p=1193396#post1193396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been struggling with one too, wasn't really sure how to approach it - but link provides some nice hooks</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I figure it would mostly revolve around having a Vampire Talmud addressing every possible &quot;How does [X] work now that I'm a vampire&quot; you could possibly think of because of <i>course</i> there'd be one of those by now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T07:29:02-07:00","id":1194240,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think that Talmudic law's the core of Judaism. That's my main issue at present, to rework the themes of Judaism into a vampire compatible faith <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:25:38-07:00","id":1194254,"title":"","content":"Well, something which could be used as the base of the Covenant is the interpretation that at Mount Sinai, God has given the Israelite two Torahs- now, according to the Rabbinic interpretation, the two Torahs are the Written and the Oral, but it could be easily played in such a way that the vampires of the Covenant (I temporary call them &quot;Sanhedrin HaDamim&quot;) believe that God gave Moses one Torah for the living, and one Torah for the dead, and just as mortals have their own rules and commandments, so does the Kindred have their own. I imagine that their official establishment would start during the days of the Second Temple, when Judaism has diverged into all kinda of cults and competing faiths. I view them as some sort of self appointed &quot;judges of the dead&quot;, who focus around teaching the Kindred how a &quot;righteous vampire&quot; is meant to act. That difference in focus may be a good way to create difference between the Sanhedrin and the Lance- for the Lancea Sanctum is focused around serving God as dark angels who test the Kine, while the Judges would focus around regulating the dead to follow God's laws. I wonder what kind of benefit the would Sanhedrin give to its members- the ideas right now move from a Kabbalistic blood magic, to a law binding ability which is similar (but different) from Carthian Laws, like certain bonuses which one would gain from following the verdicts of the Judges in the Domain, or something like that. The Covenant as whole would be, of course, Israeli, but I assume it would have certain outposts and coteries in some appropriate places (like Brooklyn).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:24:49-07:00","id":1194290,"title":"","content":"Interesting take on it.<br /> <br /> I've spend the last few reading up on things, I'll probably tie them in with the concept of Ghehenna (similar to Christian purgatory/Hell). Most people will go there for a max of twelve months. Judaic vamps would sire only by uplifting Revenants (reason: they are marked by G-D as deserving more that a twelve month stint) or, on very rare occasions, by performing a post-humous Embrace on a particularly wicked person that they reckon would rise as a Revenant anyway.<br /> <br /> Unlife in the covenant would revolve around the protection of the mortal flock, performing good deeds and striving for high levels of humanity - perhaps even Golgonda. Those who reach (say) Humanity 10 are considered cleansed. They are staked until the day the Messiah comes to resurrect the righteous from death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:05:56-07:00","id":1194575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193105-vampires-blood-and-jewish-law?p=1194254#post1194254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That difference in focus may be a good way to create difference between the Sanhedrin and the Lance- for the Lancea Sanctum is focused around serving God as dark angels who test the Kine, while the Judges would focus around regulating the dead to follow God's laws. I wonder what kind of benefit the would Sanhedrin give to its members...</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the inward focus, the fact that vampires can take banes to abridge humanity, and that that aspect of the Beast is not primarily explored by other clans or covenants, I think that could be their niche. Similar to the Ordo, the Sanhedrin chase a kind of elevation above the rest. Whereas the Ordo evolve though, the Sanhedrin regulate and restrict. As the climb in Status, the internalize more and more of God's will. This grants them the weight of the Righteous but also makes them rigid and orthodox. Kinda like Vampire Paladins, actually: lawful awesome. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Spelling errors. 03-12-2018, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:31:28-07:00","id":1194586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193105-vampires-blood-and-jewish-law?p=1194575#post1194575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the inward focus, the fact that vampires can take banes to abridge humanity, and that that aspect of the Beast is not primarily explored by other clans or covenants, I think that could be their niche. Similar to the Ordo, the Sanhedrin chase a kind of elevation above the rest. Whereas the Ordo evolve though, the Sanhedrin regulate and restrict. As the climb in Status, the internalize more and more of God's will. This grants them the weight of the Righteous but also makes them rigid and orthodox. Kinda like Vampire Paladins, actually: lawful awesome. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that could work well with the concept of buffs which work only as long as the member follows the commandments of the &quot;vampire Torah&quot;. A nice twist would be that the powers care less about the meaning of the text, and more about the interpretation- something that would give the feeling of &quot;scholarly debate&quot; which is an important aspect of Orthodox Judaism (there is a reason for the saying &quot;for every two jews you have three opinions&quot; :P). Perhaps the heads of the Covenant in the Domain are the ones to debate the exact interpretation of the commandments, and the other members of the Sanhedrin has to follow them to become &quot;righteous dead&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I would be wary of making the Sanhedrin (or any jewish derived covenant, in fact) a &quot;Gloconda cult&quot; or &quot;good guys&quot; of some kind. Vampires are, in general, not nice guys- and making the &quot;jewish Covenant&quot; as an exception to that rule would just feel weird, IMO. I want such a Covenant to be just as nasty as the other &quot;humanity aligned&quot; Covenant- and I say it as a jewish person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T12:13:02-07:00","id":1194597,"title":"","content":"Oh, yes - I should've added: that's what unlife in the covenant is said to be about. Perhaps there are even those who try. But in the end, vampires ruin everything. Still brainstorming. But it's not much different than what the Lance does: finding some form of redemption in the eyes of the lord","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}